{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והענן סר", :translit "ve-he'anan sar", :gloss "and the cloud departed"} {:he "אל תשתדל לראותו בשעת קלקלתו", :translit "al tishtadel li-r'oto bi-sh'at kilkulto", :gloss "do not strain to see Him at the time of His destruction"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Ethical maxim cited in the name of the Sages (אחז\"ל), linked to the departure of the cloud."}], :frame {:text "The cloud represents the divine presence; its departure ensured God would not witness their punishment directly. The maxim about not gazing at another's downfall appears in Eikhah Rabbah, Petichta 24, in connection with Genesis 6:9. The word קלקלתו is typically read as referring to the downfall or destruction of the person being punished.", :sources ["Eikhah Rabbah, Petichta 24"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Ethical maxim cited in the name of the Sages (אחז\"ל), linked to the departure of the cloud.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:28:36.486433138Z", :model "glm-5.2"}